{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","level":3,"text":"Required-reason APIs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What it calls","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Why none is a required-reason API","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"swift-system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"read"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resize"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unlink"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createDirectory"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setAttributes"},{"type":"text","text":" (the file protection class), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contentsOfDirectory"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isExcludedFromBackup"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager.fileExists"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data.write(to:options:)"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileVersionStore"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sysctlbyname"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.machine"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.operatingSystemVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.infoDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale.current"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NWPathMonitor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None is on the list; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":" is declared as collected data below."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracker’s record timestamps (","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s inactivity is measured between records’ wall-clock timestamps, not from the system’s uptime.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date.now"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wall-clock time, not boot time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ContinuousClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default clock of ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch()","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift runtime’s clock, which isn’t on the list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identi